<<~ ahu #/law>>

! Period Forms — what an early carrier's HUD says, and what it MUST NOT be made to say

A history carrier records how the house read at the moment it was written. ''Its instrument forms carry
as testimony'', so a sweep that modernized them in place would erase the evidence it walked through and
leave a record claiming the house always read this way.

''A carrier's HUD modernizes when it LIFTS INTO CANON, and not before.'' The Lindwyrm arc lifted and
carries current forms; the genesis-arc index stands under the same constraint and has not.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/aligned>>

!! Aligned corpus-wide

One field carries no testimony, because it names a band rather than an instrument reading:

* `meta` `register` — CODE to band-word: `CS`/`SC` → Synthesis-Canon · `PS` → Provisional-Synthesis ·
  `S` → Synthesis · `P` → Provisional · `C` → Canon

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/preserved>>

!! Preserved as period-form

These carry the early HUD verbatim. ''Read them, never rewrite them.''

```text
~:confidence[CODE],[N]   old inline confidence    → retired; the word keeps its everyday sense
✶ ◎ ◇ ■ ○                old OODA-HA phase glyphs → now  ✶ ⏿ ◇ ▶ ↺
   └ ◎/■/○ also read as STATUS (Orient / active / blocked·future) — not always phase; do NOT blind-swap
⤴  Assess / Hoʻoko       retired 6th phase        → now  folded into ↺ Hoʻoko & Aftermath
🏛️ 🌊 🗡️ 🎭 🔮 stance rows   old un-bound stance rows → now  engaged stances bind a Mu tool (🏛️/!)
```

''The status reading is the trap.'' `◎`, `■` and `○` served two axes at once in the early HUD, so a
table-driven swap from the phase column silently rewrites a blocked item as an act.

Whole-file period-artifacts stand verbatim — definitions and instructions, never narrative: the
glyph-definition drafts and the `lares-*.instructions` files.

<<~/ahu>>

